Lay-What: On a wide screen the help list and the help page each scroll on their own, and the page sits in the middle of the screen.
Lay-How: Scrolling one no longer moves the other. On a phone the help page is still a single scrolling page.
Lay-Why: The list and the page used to move together, and the page sat off to one side of the screen.
Tech-What: Desktop help gives the page list and the document each their own scroller, and centres the document on the viewport.
Tech-How: From 821px up the page body stops scrolling. The document is position fixed, width min(66ch, 760px), centred unless it would cover the list, then held at 336px. The phone layout is unchanged.
Tech-Why: Both panes shared the one scrolling page body, and a wider centred column would cover the list.
